    {
      "id": "foqv3i9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Volcanoes"
    },
    {
      "id": "y3uyrb0",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "2elkevy",
      "src": "/books/Guide/GS & GK GUIDE BOOK/images/image_2elkevy.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Volcanoes are broadly classified based on eruptive activity (active, dormant, extinct) and structural shape.",
        "Earthquakes release accumulated tectonic stress, radiating energy outward via body waves and surface waves.",
        "Seismic waves are categorized into primary (P) waves, secondary (S) waves, and surface (L) waves.",
        "Earthquake magnitude is measured logarithmically on the Richter scale, while damage intensity is assessed using the Mercalli scale.",
        "The majority of global volcanic eruptions and seismic shocks occur along the Circum-Pacific Belt."
      ],
      "id": "8iaqdfx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t3xco5i",
      "content": "A volcano is an opening in the Earth's crust through which molten rock (magma), gases, and ash are expelled to the surface. When magma reaches the Earth's surface, it is called lava."
    },
    {
      "id": "klan7nw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Structure of a Volcano"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pud8q8p",
      "content": "• Crater – bowl-shaped opening at the top of a volcano."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1mtj0jt",
      "content": "• Vent – the channel through which magma reaches the surface."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "apisil6",
      "content": "• Magma Chamber – underground reservoir of molten rock."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6p8t45r",
      "content": "• Lava Flow – molten rock flowing out during eruption."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rtghsfk",
      "content": "• Ash and Gas – volcanic eruptions release ash, steam, and gases."
    },
    {
      "id": "sqqmxs9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Volcanoes Based on Activity"
