    {
      "id": "u0hz5qg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Causes of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bo01i6v",
      "content": "• Movement of tectonic plates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4xkh337",
      "content": "• Volcanic activity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mxt1vbz",
      "content": "• Faulting in Earth's crust."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1bmsc0m",
      "content": "• Human activities such as mining and dam construction."
    },
    {
      "id": "jocnfyy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Measurement of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "id": "9cokvzv",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Scale</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Richter Scale</p>",
            "<p>Measures magnitude (energy released).</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mercalli Scale</p>",
            "<p>Measures intensity based on damage observed.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vlcvc95",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Effects of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vx3lx8c",
      "content": "• Damage to buildings and infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ceeoeb7",
      "content": "• Landslides and ground cracks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z3ym7yr",
      "content": "• Tsunamis in coastal regions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cou1yqt",
      "content": "• Loss of life and property."
    },
    {
      "id": "ueg3oj0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Major Earthquake Zones of the World"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "P-waves are compressional waves that travel through solids, liquids, and gases, whereas S-waves are shear waves that travel only through solids.",
        "The Richter Scale measures energy released (magnitude), while the Mercalli Scale measures visible destruction and impact (intensity).",
        "The Circum-Pacific Belt (Pacific Ring of Fire) accounts for nearly 68% of the world's earthquakes."
      ],
      "id": "i5z71bj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nx5p7la",
      "content": "• Pacific Ring of Fire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "urq5jpz",
      "content": "• Mid-Atlantic Ridge."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fmabcww",
      "content": "• Himalayan belt."
    },
    {
      "id": "pmo7aro",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jd0aweq",
      "content": "• Pacific Ring of Fire has the highest number of volcanoes and earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "az8o827",
      "content": "• P waves travel through solids and liquids; S waves travel only through solids."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2swqgud",
      "content": "• Epicenter is directly above the earthquake focus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7n4o8yx",
      "content": "• Richter scale measures magnitude of earthquakes."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}